m²/m³. Without a cap, even a single wood voxel per column drives τ to
essentially zero everywhere. Capping at \code{max_pad} (same value used in
\code{\link[=compute_pad_voxels]{compute_pad_voxels()}}) gives physically plausible column transmittance.

Occluded voxels (class \code{"occluded"}) are excluded from the sum and treated
as transparent (conservative — avoids inflating occlusion where pulse
sampling is unreliable). \code{NA} PAD values are also skipped (\code{na.rm = TRUE}).

